      {
        "id": 163393,
        "name": "jlabrecque42",
        "username": "jlabrecque42",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ecccb3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-23T13:49:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wager Master says \"treat that card as if it had just been played.\" Seems pretty clear cut to me that that means it should be treated as if it entered play after all the other cards, and is thus processed AFTER any previously-played face up cards.(If you ruled the other way, you could easily get into ambiguous situations where, due to the shuffling of face down cards, you didn't actually know what order the face up cards had entered play.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The alternative interpretation of \"treat that card as if it had just been played,\" is to assume that is already in play without text. &nbsp;It then turns over, stays in the same location, and the text takes effect. &nbsp;If it stays in the same location, then it's effect is resolved first and we won as stated above.</p>\n<p>The question is less about which shuffled face down card was originally played first and more about whether the face up card is played in the same location, or moved to the end of the row.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:44:24.712Z",
